# Blood Pactchinko — Project Context

## What this game is
A roguelite pachinko machine game with an occult/horror atmosphere.
The player owes a debt to the Devil and must meet a blood quota every round.
Visual style: PS1-era horror (dithering, CRT, pixel-perfect, limited palette).
Engine: Godot 4.x. Language: GDScript only.

## Core loop
1. Player starts each round with a quota of blood spheres to pay the Devil
2. Player places blood spheres into the pachinko machine pool (or sacrifices HP)
3. Player launches spheres onto the pachinko board to multiply their value
4. Devil's Gaze pressure mechanic punishes long sessions exponentially
5. Player collects win bank, pays quota, proceeds to next round
6. Shop between rounds: buy board elements, healing, inventory upgrades

## Key systems
- `SignalBus` (Autoload) — ALL cross-scene communication uses signals, never direct references
- `GameState` (Autoload) — global mutable state (current round, quota, player data)
- `PlayerData` (Resource) — HP (starts 20), blood_spheres (starts 50), gold
- `DevilsGaze` — exponential pressure scale 0-100, resets each round
- `QuotaSystem` — fixed quotas rounds 1-8, then formula-based exponential scaling
- `SphereLogic` — sphere value × element level = new value (universal formula)

## Starting values
- HP: 20 | Max HP: 20 | Starting spheres: 50 | Starting gold: 0
- 1 HP = 1 blood sphere (conversion rate, spendable in pachinko pool only)
- Devil's Gaze: BASE_INCREMENT=0.1, GROWTH_RATE=0.045 (exponential per sphere launched)
- Quota round 1: 50, round 2: 120, round 3: 250, round 4: 500 ...